<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18938" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄωρος</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, of
		the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλεκτάναι</span> or polypus-like legs of
		Scylla, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἦ τοι πόδες εἰσὶ δυώδεκα πάντες
					ἄωροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.89
				</span></i>
			; one of the Sch. expld. it as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρεμαστοί, ἀπὸ τοῦ αἰωρῶ,</span> but more prob. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκωλοι</span>
			, as Sch.HQ, from 
				Ion.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄωροι πόδες</span>
			<i>fore</i>-feet, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ τοὺς ἀώρους εἶπά σοι . . πόδας
					πρίασθαι; σὺ δὲ φέρεις ὀπισθίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philem.
					145
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
